# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .trivyignore — service-alpha
#
# Each ignored CVE MUST have a comment block documenting:
#   - Severity and affected package
#   - Why it is safe to ignore (no fix, not reachable, mitigated elsewhere)
#   - Review deadline (max 90 days from ignore date)
#
# Template:
#   # CVE-XXXX-XXXXX – <package>: <short description>
#   # Severity  : LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
#   # Status    : <no upstream fix | fix pending | mitigated by ...>
#   # Scope     : <which binary/path is affected and why it's not reachable>
#   # Review by : YYYY-MM-DD
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2023-4641 – shadow-utils: newgrp leaks passwords to the audit subsystem
# Severity  : LOW
# Status    : No upstream fix available as of 2025-05-01 (Debian bookworm)
# Scope     : Affects /usr/sbin/newgrp. This binary is not present in the
#             runtime image and the service never calls newgrp at runtime.
# Review by : 2025-08-01
CVE-2023-4641
